questions.explanationText:
Given, $$D = \left| {\matrix{
1 & 1 & 1 \cr
1 & {1 + x} & 1 \cr
1 & 1 & {1 + y} \cr

} } \right|$$

Apply $$\,\,\,{R^2} \to {R_2} - {R_1}$$ $$\,\,\,\,$$

and $$\,\,\,\,$$ $$R \to {R_3} - {R_1}$$

$$\therefore$$ $$\,\,\,\,\,D = \left| {\matrix{
1 & 1 & 1 \cr
0 & x & 0 \cr
0 & 0 & y \cr

} } \right| = xy$$

Hence, $$D$$ is divisible by both $$x$$ and $$y$$

